From 1753bb04b4447148bbc7526981113f08d6ce0361 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elena Popa <elena.popa@nxp.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Oct 2025 16:40:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] imx9:scmi:soc: remove the ft_add_optee_node call from SPL

When U-Boot proper is skipped, the ft_system_setup() function must be
called in SPL. This function calls, in turn, the ft_add_optee_node(),
which will not execute correctly, because at that point, rom_pointer is
not initialized with the correct values.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific Falcon Mode support]

Signed-off-by: Elena Popa <elena.popa@nxp.com>
---
 arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/scmi/soc.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/scmi/soc.c b/arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/scmi/soc.c
index 4cf0bc46ebf..73e0b4cc8c6 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/scmi/soc.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-imx/imx9/scmi/soc.c
@@ -1350,7 +1350,11 @@ int ft_system_setup(void *blob, struct bd_info *bd)
 				"kaslr-seed", fdt_strerror(ret));
 	}
 
+#if defined(CONFIG_SPL_BUILD)
+	return 0;
+#else
 	return ft_add_optee_node(blob, bd);
+#endif
 }
 
 /* Fix uboot dtb based on fuses. */
-- 
2.34.1

